Day12
Problem statement: Troubleshoot why application deployed on one server is not accessible from Jump server. Application is using Apache webserver.

1. First we will login into server on which this application is deployed using below command. Provide required password when prompted.
        ssh username@hostname
2. Let's check status of the Apache service using below command
        sudo systemctl status httpd
3. In ouptut, I found that service was not running. Hence, I tried to start service using below command. But, service could not start.
        sudo systemctl start httpd.
4. In the output of above command, I found that there was one error with "Address already in use"
5. I tried to use netstat to investigate but netstat was not available or installed. Hence, installed using below command
        sudo yum install net-tools -y
6. Once installation was completed, tried below command to check which services is using particular port. As port 5002 was being assigned to application deployed on Apache webserver.
        sudo netstat -tulpn | grep 5002        
7. The output of above command confirmed that service sendmail was using same port instead of default port 25.
8. I had edit sendmail.mc file under /etc/mail to configure port 25 using below command. This basically opens sendmail.mc file in editor and you will need to search port, update and then save the file.
        sudo vi /etc/mail/sendmail.mc
9. I restarted sendmail service using below service
        sudo systemctl restart sendmail.
10. I tried restarting httpd service using below command and service was in running state.
        sudo systemctl restart httpd                
11. However, but still application was not accessible from Jump server.
12. To troubleshoot next, I tried to check firewalld service but it was not installed. Then, I checked iptables using below command
        sudo iptables -L        
13. The output of above command confirmed that there was some misconfiguration which was blocking traffic to port 5002. Below is the output for reference.

Chain INPUT (policy ACCEPT)
target     prot opt source               destination         
ACCEPT     all  --  anywhere             anywhere             state RELATED,ESTABLISHED
ACCEPT     icmp --  anywhere             anywhere            
ACCEPT     all  --  anywhere             anywhere            
ACCEPT     tcp  --  anywhere             anywhere             state NEW tcp dpt:ssh
REJECT     all  --  anywhere             anywhere             reject-with icmp-host-prohibited        
14. This explained that traffic was blocked.
15. I updated iptables to enable traffic on port 5002 using below command
        sudo iptables -I INPUT 5 -p tcp --dport 5002 -j ACCEPT
16. After this service was accessible from Jump server.        